Today is Thursday evening at half past five.
I go to the sports club.
First, I go to the front desk.
"Please give me a racket," I say to the staff member.
He gives the racket, and I pay the rent.
Then I enter the court.
Neha is already present there.
We smile and greet each other.
"Maya, are you ready today?" Neha asks with a laugh.
"I am completely ready," I reply.
Our badminton match begins.
We play highly competitively.
Neha plays very well.
But I also score many points.
Between points, we casually tease each other.
"Maya, that is a good shot!" she says.
"Thank you, but today I am going to win," I say smiling.
This badminton match is very enjoyable.
Playing with Neha is my favourite part of Thursday.
